        <item>
            <title>Captin 2.0.4</title>
            <description>
                <![CDATA[
                    <h1>Version 2.0.4</h1>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Notarized release so Gatekeeper accepts the app on first launch after download.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr>
                    <h1>Version 2.0.3</h1>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Preferences window appears frontmost when launching from Finder with Dock icon hidden.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr>
                    <h1>Version 2.0.2</h1>
                    <ul>
                    <li>HUD display position (X and Y) now persists correctly after restart.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr>
                    <h1>Version 2.0.1</h1>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Dock icon and menu bar icon preferences are saved correctly after restart.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr>
                    <h1>Version 2.0</h1>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Rewritten entirely in Swift.</li>
                    <li>Various minor improvements.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Requires macOS 11.5 (Big Sur) or later. If your Mac is on macOS 10.13&ndash;11.4, please stay on version 1.3.1 and do not upgrade. <strong>Click Learn More… to download Captin 2.0.4.</strong></p>
                    <hr>
                    <h1>Version 1.3.1</h1>
                    <h2>Added:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Support Apple CPU.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <h2>Improved:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>User experience.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr>
                    <h1>Version 1.3</h1>
                    <h2>Added:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Restore default setting.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <h2>Improved:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Monitor information fetching.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr>
                    <h1>Version 1.2.1</h1>
                    <h2>Fixed:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Compatibility issue on Mac Ventura.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr>
                    <h1>Version 1.2</h1>
                    <h2>Added:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>New way to position HUD window.<p>Captin can position HUD window centered on screen in horizontal or vertical direction, or set an offset for HUD window in horizontal or vertical direction.</p></li>
                    </ul>
                    <h2>Improved:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Captin is now notarized by Apple.</li>
                    <li>HUD can be placed on any position on screen, including menu bar.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <h2>Fixed:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Compatibility issue on macOS Ventura.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr>
                    <h1>Version 1.1.7</h1>
                    <h2>Fixed:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Do not show input method change notification repeatedly.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr>
                    <h1>Version 1.1.6</h1>
                    <h2>Fixed:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Caps lock status is changed to off when the user switches to another input method.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <h2>Updated:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Display information for compatibility.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr>
                    <h1>Version 1.1.5</h1>
                    <h2>Fixed:</h2>
                    <ul>
                    <li>Issue on some models that can not get display preview info.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <hr>
                    <p>For issue or question about our app, please mail us: <a href="mailto:support@100hps.com">support@100hps.com</a></p>
                ]]>
            </description>
            <pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:18:44 +0800</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>207</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.0.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>11.5</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
